Never request an ACK_FREQUENCY max ack delay below the peer's min_ack_delay

Applies to picoquic 70b5fd5aafdd2d6c349ff783202ece9d778bcaf2, after 0001 to
0011.

picoquic_compute_ack_gap_and_delay() corrects the requested max ack delay when
the return path is slow, then caps it at PICOQUIC_ACK_DELAY_MAX (10 ms). If the
peer advertised a min_ack_delay above 10 ms, which quicly does with 25 ms, that
cap can produce an ACK_FREQUENCY request below the peer's min_ack_delay. This
happens when there is some queueing and the return data rate is low. The peer
then closes the connection with PROTOCOL_VIOLATION on frame type 0xaf. After
the cap, the delay is now raised back to remote_min_ack_delay.

Upstream: PR2369, merged as 36f49b73d532369882d97474ac018655b6739a58. This is
the same change, backported. Remove this patch once the pin includes that
commit.

Test: ackfrq_min_delay (ack_frequency_test.c) sets a 25 ms remote
min_ack_delay and a 2000 B/s receive rate, which triggers the correction and
the 10 ms cap. The requested max ack delay must not be lower than the remote
min_ack_delay. Without the fix it fails; with the fix it passes.

